hadiths[33]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15499","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Qatadah narrated to us, from Kathir, from Abu Iyad, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting between the sun and the shade, and said: It is the sitting place of Satan."
"15500","Mutamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep until he breathed heavily, then he stood and prayed and did not perform wudu."
"15502","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from a man of the people of Makkah called Yusuf, he said: I and a man of Quraysh were in charge of the property of orphans, he said: And a man had taken a thousand dirhams belonging to me, he said: Then a thousand dirhams belonging to him came into my hands, he said: So I said to the Qurashi: He took a thousand dirhams of mine, and I have got hold of a thousand dirhams of his, he said: Then the Qurashi said: My father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."
"15574","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Musab, he said: A man of the people of Madinah came, an old man, and they saw him affecting his equipment. So they asked him, and he told them that he intends al-Maghrib, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will go out to al-Maghrib, coming on the Day of Resurrection with their faces upon the light of the sun."
"15736","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr and Abu Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Za'idah narrated to us, he said: al-Sa'ib ibn Hubaysh al-Kala'i narrated to us, from Abu al-Shammakh al-Azdi, from a cousin of his among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who came to Mu'awiyah and entered upon him, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is entrusted with an affair of the people then closes his door against the poor and the oppressed or the needy, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will close the doors of His mercy against him at his need and poverty when he is most in need of it."
"15737","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, that a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you is in his prayer, let him not raise his sight to the heaven, lest his sight be snatched away."
"15894","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrating from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: One who saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment with its ends crossed informed me."
"15895","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, he said: Alqamah al-Muzani narrated to me, he said: A man narrated to me, he said: I was in a gathering in which was Umar ibn al-Khattab in Madinah. He said to a man of the people: O so-and-so, how did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, describe Islam? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Islam began as a jadha, then a thaniyya, then a rabaiya, then a sudasiya, then a bazil. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: After full maturity there is only decline."
"15988","Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid, meaning Isma'il, narrated to us, from his father, he said: I entered upon a man eating milk mixed with dates, and he said: Come near, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named them the two most wholesome."
"15989","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhad Abu Umar, he said, one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, saying: Whoever is prompted at death with there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"15990","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Sa'ib, from a man of Bakr ibn Wa'il, from his maternal uncle, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I take tithes from my people? He said: Tithes are only upon the Jews and Christians; there are no tithes upon the people of Islam."
"15991","He said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata, from Harb ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, from his maternal uncle, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned things to him and asked him. So he said: Shall I tithe them? So he said: Tithes are only upon the Jews and Christians; there are no tithes upon the people of Islam."
"15992","Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Harb ibn Hilal al-Thaqafi, from the father of his mother, a man of Banu Taghlib: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are no tithes upon the Muslims; tithes are only upon the Jews and Christians."
"15993","Mu'awiya ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Za'ida narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: How do you say in prayer? He said: I recite the tashahhud, then say: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek refuge with You from the Fire. But I do not do well your humming nor the humming of Mu'adh. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Around it we hum."
"15998","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said, Malik informed me, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded people to break the fast in the year of the conquest, and said: Strengthen yourselves against your enemy. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted. Abu Bakr said: The one who narrated to me said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Arj pouring water over his head from thirst or heat. Then it was said: O Messenger of Allah, a group of people fasted when you fasted. When he was at al-Kadid, he called for a cup and drank, and the people broke the fast."
"15999","He said: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sa'd, meaning Ibn Aws al-Absi, narrated to us, from Bilal al-Absi, he said, Imran ibn Husayn al-Dabbi informed us: that he came to Basra, with Abd Allah ibn Abbas as governor there, and there was a man standing in the shade of the palace saying: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, adding nothing to that. So I drew near him somewhat and said to him: You have repeated your saying Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. So he said: By Allah, if you wish, I shall inform you. So I said: Yes. So he said: Sit then. So he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Madina at such-and-such time, and two elders of the tribe had a son of theirs who had gone and joined him. So they said: You are going to Madina, and a son of ours has joined this man, so go to him and seek him from him, and if he refuses but ransom, then ransom him. So I came to Madina and entered upon the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Prophet of Allah, two elders of the tribe commanded me to seek a son of theirs with you. So he said: Do you know him? So he said: I know his lineage. So he called the boy, and he came. So he said: Here he is, take him to his parents. So I said: Ransom, O Prophet of Allah. He said: It is not proper for us, the family of Muhammad, to eat the price of anyone of the children of Isma'il. Then he struck my shoulder, then said: I fear for Quraysh nothing but themselves. I said: What is with them, O Prophet of Allah? He said: If your life is long, you will see them here until you see people between them like sheep between two troughs, once to this and once to this. And I see people seeking permission from Ibn Abbas; I saw them this year seeking permission from Mu'awiya, so I remembered what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"16033","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, from a man who was old, of Banu Tamim, who was in the time of Uthman, a man informing from his father that he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, write for me a document that I not be taken for the offense of another, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: That is for you and for every Muslim."
"16037","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, he said, al-Saib ibn Hubaysh narrated to us, from Abu al-Shammakh al-Azdi, from a cousin of his of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he came to Muawiyah and entered upon him and said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is put in charge of the affairs of the people, then closes his door against the needy, or the wronged, or the one in need, Allah, mighty and majestic, closes against him the doors of His mercy at his need and his poverty, most poor as he is to it."
"16038","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said, Sharik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said, a man of the people of Syria called on the day of Siffin: Is Uways al-Qarani among you, they said: Yes, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Among the best of the followers is Uways al-Qarani."
"16172","He said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari informed me, and he is one of the three who were forgiven, that one of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day binding his head, and said in his sermon: As for after, O company of Muhajirun, you have become increasing, and the Ansar have become not increasing over their state which they are upon today. And the Ansar are my chest to which I sheltered. So honor their noble and overlook their wrongdoer."
"16320","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from the man who passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was conversing privately with Jibril, peace be upon him, and Abu Salamah claimed that he avoided approaching the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fearing to hear his hadith. So when morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you from greeting when you passed by me last night? He said: I saw you conversing privately with a man, and I feared you would dislike that I approach you both. He said: And do you know who the man is? He said: No. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him, and had you greeted, he would have returned the greeting. And I have heard from other than Abu Salamah that he was Harithah ibn al-Nu'man."
"16321","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrating, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: One who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a garment whose ends he had crossed informed me."
"16526","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from one of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The best speech is: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great."
"20550","Isma'il informed us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-'Ala', he said: A man said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and the people were taking turns, and mounts were few; my turn to dismount with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and my turn, then he caught up with me from behind and struck my shoulder, saying: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. So I said: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited it, and I recited it with him. Then he said: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited it, and I recited it with him. He said: When you pray, recite them both."
"20630","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Salil, he said: A man stood over us in our gathering at al-Baqi' and said: My father or my uncle narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Baqi' saying: Who will give charity with which I will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: So I loosened a winding or two windings from my turban, intending to give them in charity, then what overtakes the sons of Adam overtook me and I tied my turban on me. Then a man came, and I never saw at al-Baqi' a man more intensely black and yellow than him, nor darker, leading a she-camel, and I never saw at al-Baqi' a she-camel better than it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is it charity? He said: Yes. He said: Take this she-camel. He said: A man clung to him and said: This one gives this in charity, and by Allah it is better than him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard it and said: You have lied, rather he is better than you and than it, three times. Then he said: Woe to the owners of the hundreds of camels, three times. They said: Except whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Except one who says with wealth thus and thus, and he joined his two palms to his right and to his left. Then he said: Successful is the ascetic striving one, three times, the ascetic in livelihood, the striving in worship."
"20862","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ishaq ibn Suwayd, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There was an amir in Kufa, he said: So he preached one day and said: In giving this wealth there is trial, and in withholding it there is trial, and with that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in his sermon until he finished, then he descended."
"20866","Abu Mu'awiyah and Abadah narrated to us, both said: Asim narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, he said: One who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, he said: Give every surah its share of bowing and prostration."
"21016","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Budayl al-Uqayli, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq informed me, that one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him, while he was at Wadi al-Qura and upon his horse, and a man from Bulqayn asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these? He said: these are those who earned anger, and he pointed to the Jews. Then he said: who are these? He said: these are the astray, meaning the Christians. He said: and a man came to him and said: your freedman, or he said your boy, so-and-so, has been martyred. He said: rather he is being dragged into the Fire in a cloak he stole."
"21024","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from a man of his people, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and said: recite with them in your prayer, with the two Muawwidhat (Surat al-Falaq and Surat al-Nas)."
"21025","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala, he said: a man said: we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the people were taking turns, and riding animals were few. The dismounting time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my dismounting time came, then he caught up with me from behind me and struck my shoulder and said: say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. So I said: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it and I recited it with him. Then he said: say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it and I recited it with him. Then he said: when you pray, recite with them."
"21028","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: one of the companions of Muhammad narrated to me, and we had raided toward Persia, and he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever sleeps on a roof that has no railing, then falls and dies, then protection is removed from him. And whoever rides the sea when it is turbulent and dies, then protection is removed from him."
"21029","Azhar narrated to us, Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: we were in Persia, and over us was a commander called Zuhayr ibn Abdullah, and he said: a man narrated to me that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever sleeps on a railing, or on a roof around which there is nothing to stop his leg, then protection is removed from him. And whoever rides the sea after it becomes turbulent, then protection is removed from him."
"21046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, he said: I heard Abu Qilabah narrating, from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: do you recite while the imam recites? Or he said: do you recite behind the imam while the imam recites? They said: yes. He said: then do not do so, except that one of you recites the Opening of the Book to himself. Khalid said: and he narrated to me after, and he did not say if he wishes, so I said to Abu Qilabah: if he wishes? He said: I do not remember it."
